2.4 General Constraints
•	CO-1: The system must be developed using standard web technologies including HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript for the frontend, and Node.js (Express.js) for backend processing, with MongoDB as the primary database.
•	CO-2: The system must run on standard web browsers and must be compatible with Google Chrome (v90+), Mozilla Firefox (v85+), and Microsoft Edge (v88+) without additional plugins or software.
•	CO-3: The chatbot functionality is strictly limited to predefined responses stored in the MongoDB database and does not include advanced artificial intelligence or natural language processing capabilities in the initial version.
•	CO-4: The system depends on a stable internet connection and proper server configuration for correct operation, performance, and data integrity.
•	CO-5: The system shall not include online payment gateway integration in the initial version. Order placement confirms intent to purchase, and payment processing is handled offline.
•	CO-6: All user-uploaded data and product images shall be stored within the server filesystem and shall not exceed 5 MB per file.

2.5 Assumptions and Dependencies
•	AS-1: It is assumed that users will have access to a stable internet connection and a compatible, up-to-date web browser.
•	AS-2: The system depends on the availability of a properly configured server environment, including the Node.js runtime, Express.js framework, and MongoDB database. Any issues in these components may affect system performance.
•	AS-3: It is assumed that administrators will provide accurate and complete product information when adding or updating the product catalog.
•	AS-4: FAQ responses stored in the database are assumed to be pre-populated and maintained by the system administrator to ensure chatbot accuracy.
•	AS-5: The system assumes users will provide valid and accurate information during registration and order placement.

 
3. Specific Requirements
This section presents the most important and detailed requirements of the SRS. The customer requirements captured in Section 2 are elaborated here as D-requirements that guide the project's software design, implementation, and testing. Each requirement in this section is correct, traceable, unambiguous, verifiable, prioritized, complete, consistent, and uniquely identifiable through a systematic numbering scheme.

3.1 External Interface Requirements
3.1.1 System Interfaces
The system interacts with a MongoDB database for storing and retrieving all persistent data, including user accounts, product details, order records, shopping cart data, and chatbot FAQ entries. The application server layer (Node.js/Express.js) communicates with MongoDB via the Mongoose ODM (Object Document Mapper) to ensure structured and validated data access.

3.1.2 Interfaces
The system provides a graphical user interface (GUI) accessible through standard web browsers. The interface is designed to be responsive, simple, and easy to use across desktop and mobile devices. It includes separate interface views for general users (shopping interface with chatbot) and administrators (management dashboard). All UI components are built using HTML5, CSS3, and Bootstrap 5 to ensure consistency and accessibility.

3.1.3 Hardware Interfaces
The system has no specific hardware interface requirements beyond a standard internet-connected computing device (desktop, laptop, tablet, or smartphone) capable of running a modern web browser. No proprietary hardware or peripheral devices are required for the operation of this system.

3.1.4 Software Interfaces
The system uses the following software interfaces and components:
•	Node.js (v18.x or higher) with Express.js framework for server-side application logic and RESTful API routing.
•	MongoDB (v6.x or higher) as the primary NoSQL database for all data persistence and retrieval.
•	Mongoose ODM library for structured MongoDB schema definition and data validation.
•	Modern web browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Edge) as the client-side runtime environment for rendering the user interface.
•	Bootstrap 5 CSS framework for responsive frontend design and UI component styling.

3.1.5 Communications Interfaces
The system uses HTTP/HTTPS protocols to communicate between the client browser and the Node.js application server over the internet. All sensitive data transmissions, including user login credentials, registration information, and order details, shall be secured using HTTPS (TLS 1.2 or higher). RESTful API endpoints are used for asynchronous communication between the frontend and backend, including chatbot query processing and real-time cart updates.

 
