The following section presents the Use Case Diagram and detailed use case descriptions for the E-Commerce Website with FAQs Chatbot Integration. The diagram was developed following UML standards and depicts all major actor-system interactions for both the User and Administrator roles.

3.3.1 Use Case Diagram

Figure 1 below illustrates the complete Use Case Diagram for the E-Commerce Website with FAQs Chatbot Integration. The diagram shows two primary actors — User and Admin — and all their respective interactions with the system, including the sequential flow from product browsing through order placement, and the independent chatbot interaction path.

 
Figure 1: Use Case Diagram – E-Commerce Website with FAQs Chatbot Integration

As illustrated in Figure 1, the system encompasses two distinct actors and their respective use cases:
•	User Actor: Interacts with the system through Register Account, Login, Browse Products, View Product Details (which flows from Browse Products), Manage Cart (which flows from View Product Details), Place Order (which flows from Manage Cart), and Interact with Chatbot (which leads to Get FAQ Response).
•	Admin Actor: Interacts with the system through Admin Login, Add Product, Update Product, Delete Product, and Manage Orders.
