3.5 Non-Functional Requirements
This section specifies the non-functional requirements of the E-Commerce Website with FAQs Chatbot Integration. These requirements define the quality attributes and operational constraints that the system must exhibit, including performance, reliability, availability, security, maintainability, and portability.

3.5.1 Performance
•	PER-1: 95% of all web pages generated by the system shall load completely within 3 seconds over a 10 Mbps or faster internet connection under normal operating load.
•	PER-2: The system shall support at least 100 concurrent user sessions without significant performance degradation (response time increase of no more than 20% from baseline).
•	PER-3: Product search and filtering queries shall return results within 2 seconds for a catalog containing up to 5,000 product records.
•	PER-4: Chatbot FAQ query matching and response delivery shall complete within 1 second of user query submission.
•	PER-5: Order placement processing shall complete and return a confirmation to the user within 2 seconds of submission.

3.5.2 Reliability
•	REL-1: The system shall operate without failures and maintain data consistency during all read and write operations, using MongoDB's atomic transactions for critical operations such as order placement and stock decrement.
•	REL-2: The system shall perform automated database backups every 24 hours to prevent data loss in the event of a server failure.
•	REL-3: In the event of a server-side error, the system shall display a user-friendly error page and log error details for administrator review, without exposing sensitive technical information.
•	REL-4: The system shall handle concurrent write operations (e.g., multiple simultaneous order placements) without data corruption or race conditions.

3.5.3 Availability
•	AVL-1: The system shall be available at all times except during planned maintenance windows, targeting an uptime of at least 99% on a monthly basis.
•	AVL-2: Planned maintenance windows shall be scheduled during off-peak hours and communicated to users at least 24 hours in advance via a website notice.
•	AVL-3: The chatbot functionality shall remain available independently of other system modules where technically feasible.

3.5.4 Security
•	SEC-1: The system shall encrypt all user passwords using bcrypt hashing with a minimum salt factor of 10 before storing them in the database. Plain-text passwords shall never be stored.
•	SEC-2: All data transmission between the client browser and the server shall be secured using HTTPS (TLS 1.2 or higher) to prevent interception of sensitive user data.
•	SEC-3: The system shall implement protection against Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks by sanitizing all user-provided inputs before rendering them in the browser.
•	SEC-4: The system shall enforce role-based access control (RBAC), ensuring that general users and administrators can only access features corresponding to their assigned role.
•	SEC-5: All API endpoints that perform state-changing operations (POST, PUT, DELETE) shall require a valid authenticated session token to process the request.
•	SEC-6: User sessions shall expire after 30 minutes of inactivity, requiring re-authentication to resume.

3.5.5 Maintainability
•	MNT-1: The system code shall be organized into modular components separated by function (routes, controllers, models, middleware) following the MVC (Model-View-Controller) architectural pattern to facilitate independent development and maintenance.
•	MNT-2: All code shall be documented with inline comments following standard JavaScript documentation conventions to enable future developers to understand, modify, and extend the system.
•	MNT-3: The system shall be version-controlled using Git, with all changes committed with descriptive messages to maintain a clear and traceable development history.
•	MNT-4: The FAQ database shall be maintainable by the administrator through the admin dashboard without requiring code-level changes.

3.5.6 Portability
•	POR-1: The system shall work correctly on all major web browsers including Google Chrome (v90+), Mozilla Firefox (v85+), and Microsoft Edge (v88+) without layout or functional issues.
•	POR-2: The system's responsive interface shall adapt correctly to screen resolutions ranging from 320px (mobile) to 1920px (desktop) without loss of functionality or readability.
•	POR-3: The server-side application shall be portable across Linux-based operating systems (Ubuntu 20.04 LTS or higher) and Windows Server environments that support Node.js runtime.

 
3.6 Inverse Requirements
Inverse requirements define what the system will explicitly NOT do or support in its current version. These boundaries are important for managing stakeholder expectations and preventing scope creep during development.

•	INV-1: The system will NOT include advanced artificial intelligence (AI) or natural language processing (NLP) features for the chatbot in the initial version. All chatbot responses are limited to predefined FAQ database entries.
•	INV-2: The system will NOT integrate a live online payment gateway (e.g., Stripe, PayPal) in the initial version. Order placement confirms purchase intent, and payment is handled offline.
•	INV-3: The system will NOT support real-time inventory synchronization with external supplier or warehouse management systems.
•	INV-4: The system will NOT provide a mobile application (iOS or Android). The initial version is web-only, accessible through mobile browsers via the responsive interface.
•	INV-5: The system will NOT include a user product review or rating feature in the initial version.
•	INV-6: The system will NOT support multi-vendor or marketplace functionality. All products are managed by a single administrator.

3.7 Logical Database Requirements
The system shall use a MongoDB NoSQL database to store all persistent data. MongoDB's document-oriented storage model is well-suited for the variable and nested data structures required by the e-commerce system. The following logical collections and their relationships define the database schema:

Collection	Key Fields	Relationships
Users	userID, fullName, email, passwordHash, isActive	One-to-Many with Orders, One-to-One with Cart
Products	productID, name, price, category, stockQuantity, imageURL	Referenced in Cart items and Order orderedItems
Cart	cartID, userID, items[], totalPrice	Many-to-One with Users; items reference Products
Orders	orderID, userID, orderedItems[], totalAmount, orderStatus	Many-to-One with Users; orderedItems snapshot Products
FAQs	faqID, question, answer, keywords[]	Independent collection; queried by chatbot module
Admins	adminID, username, passwordHash	Independent collection; separate from Users

Data integrity is maintained through Mongoose schema validation at the application layer, ensuring all required fields are present and correctly typed before records are persisted to the database.

3.8 Design Constraints
The following design constraints govern the architectural and implementation decisions of the E-Commerce Website with FAQs Chatbot Integration:

•	DC-1: The system shall be developed using Node.js (Express.js) for the backend, HTML5/CSS3/JavaScript with Bootstrap 5 for the frontend, and MongoDB for the database. No other primary backend or database technologies are permitted in the initial version.
•	DC-2: The system shall follow the MVC (Model-View-Controller) architectural pattern, separating business logic (controllers), data access (models), and user interface (views/templates) into distinct modules.
•	DC-3: The system shall use RESTful API design principles for all client-server communication, including standard HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE) and appropriate HTTP status codes.
•	DC-4: All user-uploaded files (product images) shall be stored in the server's designated upload directory and must not exceed 5 MB per file. Only standard image formats (JPEG, PNG, WebP) are accepted.
•	DC-5: The project shall be version-controlled using Git with a structured branching strategy (main, development, feature branches) throughout the development lifecycle.

3.8.1 Standards Compliance
The system shall follow the following standards and best practices to ensure quality, security, and interoperability:

